"""fig3c_cross_scale_similarity_pearson.csv | main Fig. 3 (04_figures/fig.3/fig3_main_A4_v2.py)

Recovered statistical-analysis script | reproducibility package | Fig. 3 track.

WHAT THIS SCRIPT COMPUTES
    This code builds a symmetric cross-scale similarity matrix comparing
    functional connectivity edge profiles derived from different
    simulation or acquisition scales (3m_268, 10m_268, 10m_1000, 10m_own,
    10m, 100m, 1b), where each scale's profile is the subject-averaged
    mean across repeated runs of a fixed set of 12 edges under a baseline
    condition. For each pair of scales, it computes the Pearson
    correlation coefficient between their flattened mean edge profiles,
    setting the diagonal to 1.0 by construction. One row of the output
    table corresponds to a single scale and reports its Pearson
    correlation with every scale in the same fixed order, so the row is a
    vector of similarity values between that scale's edge profile and each
    of the seven scales' edge profiles.

INPUT FILES
    {B}/revision/10m_voxel_population_simulation/simulate_FC_edges.csv
    {B}/revision/model_scale_consistent/NP_12edges_10m_1000_10m_268_regional_modu.csv
    {MN}/NP_12edges_all_subjects_scales_conditions_newflow.csv
    {R3}/Baseline_simulated_NP_12edges_and_factor_3m_new_run.mat
    {VX}/new10m_simulated_FC_12subs_with_empirical.mat

OUTPUT FILE
    fig3c_cross_scale_similarity_pearson.csv
    written to OUT_DIR (default /tmp/recovery_scratch/fig3)
    reference copy in this package: 04_figures/fig.3/fig3_data/fig3c_cross_scale_similarity_pearson.csv

STATISTICAL TESTS
    Pearson correlation

RUNNABLE ON A LAPTOP
    conditional on the input files above being present on this machine

SEED
    not applicable (deterministic computation)

